              <xs:documentation>The price of the product. It supports the following formats: \&quot;24.99 USD\&quot;, \&quot;24.99USD\&quot; and \&quot;24.99\&quot;. If the currency is not included, we default to US dollars.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="product_type" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;&#x3D; 1000 characters. The categorization of your product based on your custom product taxonomy. Subcategories must be sent separated by \&quot; &gt; \&quot;.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="promotion_id" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>A unique identifier referencing the promotion associated with this catalog item.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="sale_price" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>The discounted price of the product. The sale_price must be lower than the price. It supports the following formats: \&quot;14.99 USD\&quot;, \&quot;14.99USD\&quot; and \&quot;14.99\&quot;.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="sale_price_effective_date" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>Sale price effective date. Expected format: &lt;start_date&gt;/&lt;end_date&gt; (ISO 8601 format)</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="shipping" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>Shipping consists of one group of up to four elements, country, region, service (all optional) and price (required). All colons, even for blank values, are required.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="shipping_height" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>The height of the package needed to ship the product. Ensure there is a space between the numeric string and the metric.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="shipping_weight" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>The weight of the product. Ensure there is a space between the numeric string and the metric.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="shipping_width" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>The width of the package needed to ship the product. Ensure there is a space between the numeric string and the metric.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="size" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>The size of the product.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="size_system" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>Indicates the country&#39;s sizing system in which you are submitting your product. Must be one of the following values (upper or lowercased): &#39;US&#39;, &#39;UK&#39;, &#39;EU&#39;, &#39;DE&#39;, &#39;FR&#39;, &#39;JP&#39;, &#39;CN&#39;, &#39;IT&#39;, &#39;BR&#39;, &#39;MEX&#39;, or &#39;AU&#39;.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="size_type" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>Additional description for the size. Must be one of the following values (upper or lowercased): &#39;regular&#39;, &#39;petite&#39;, &#39;plus&#39;, &#39;big_and_tall&#39;, or &#39;maternity&#39;.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="tax" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>Tax consists of one group of up to four elements, country, region, rate (all required) and tax_ship (optional). All colons, even for blank values, are required.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="title" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;&#x3D; 500 characters. The name of the product.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="unit_pricing_base_measure" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>Unit pricing base measure of the product. Expected format: &lt;base_measure&gt; &lt;unit_type&gt;</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="unit_pricing_measure" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>Unit pricing total measure of the product. Expected format: &lt;total_units&gt; &lt;unit_type&gt;</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" name="variant_names" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>Options for this variant. People will see these options next to your Pin and can select the one they want. List them in the order you want them displayed.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" name="variant_values" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>Option values for this variant. People will see these options next to your Pin and can select the one they want. List them in the order you want them displayed. The order of the variant values must be consistent with the order of the variant names.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
        </xs:sequence>
